-- חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ט/9: עדכון חוזר לבעלויות תשע"ה/2 בנושא תוכנית היבחנות חדשה בבחינת הבגרות בחטיבה העליונה
-- Circular תשע"ה/2 split the matriculation (bagrut) preparation reward of
-- each subject between the external examination and the school-based
-- assessment. This circular updates the split in four subjects from school
-- year תש"פ (1.9.2019): the attached table gives each one's reward, its
-- external and school-based parts, and how a part is divided between two
-- examination events.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT common

§ `חוזר תשע"ט/9 עדכון חלוקת גמול הבגרות`

-- akn:hc_1/p1 akn:hc_1/p2 akn:hc_1/p3 akn:hc_1/p4 akn:hc_1/p5 akn:hc_1/p6 akn:hc_1/p7 akn:hc_1/p8 akn:hc_1/p9 akn:hc_1/p10 akn:hc_1/p11 akn:hc_1/p12 akn:hc_1/p13 The letterhead, date, reference, addressee, greeting and subject line; no rule.

-- akn:hc_1/p14 akn:hc_1/p15 The recital: circular תשע"ה/2 published a table splitting the bagrut reward between the external examination and the school-based assessment; the updated rows are encoded below.

-- akn:hc_1/p18 akn:hc_1/p19 akn:hc_1/p20 akn:hc_1/p21 akn:hc_1/p22 akn:hc_1/p23 akn:hc_1/p24 akn:hc_1/p25 akn:hc_1/p26 akn:hc_1/p27 akn:hc_1/p28 akn:hc_1/p29 akn:hc_1/p30 akn:hc_1/p31 akn:hc_1/p32 akn:hc_1/p33 akn:hc_1/p34 akn:hc_1/p35 akn:hc_1/p36 akn:hc_1/p37 akn:hc_1/p38 akn:hc_1/p39 akn:hc_1/p40 akn:hc_1/p41 akn:hc_1/p42 akn:hc_1/p43 The sign-off and the copies list (the corpus holds them inside the body); no rule.

-- ¶17: the updates apply from school year תש"פ, 1.9.2019.
@ref akn:hc_1/p17
`the updates apply from` MEANS Date 1 9 2019

GIVEN `the school year begins` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the updated split applies to the year beginning` `the school year begins` IF
    `the school year begins` AT LEAST `the updates apply from`

§§ `הטבלה: מקצועות ההוראה בהם חלו עדכונים בחלוקה הפנימית`

-- The attached table. Its columns, as the corpus prints the headings
-- (¶46-¶50): the subject and its study units; for geography and Land-of-
-- Israel studies the part of the examination (the questionnaire, or the
-- geotop field project); the reward "before the reform" in weekly hours
-- (ש"ש) and in percent; and the reward "in the reform", split into the
-- external examination and the school-based assessment, each in weekly
-- hours and in percent. "The reform" is read as the new examination plan
-- the subject line names. A blank cell is NOTHING: the table gives no
-- figure there.
@desc A row of the attached table.
DECLARE `reward row` HAS
    `subject`                       IS A STRING
    `study units`                   IS A NUMBER
    `examination part`              IS A STRING @desc "שאלון" (questionnaire) or "גיאוטופ" (geotop); "" where the row is the whole subject
    `before the reform, weekly hours` IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `before the reform, percent`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `external, weekly hours`        IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `external, percent`             IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `school-based, weekly hours`    IS A MAYBE NUMBER
    `school-based, percent`         IS A MAYBE NUMBER

DECLARE `part of the reward` IS ONE OF
    `the external examination`
    `the school-based assessment`

DECLARE `unit of the reward` IS ONE OF
    `weekly hours`
    `percent`

DECLARE `reward action` IS ONE OF
    `pay the reward for the part` HAS `reward paid` IS A NUMBER

-- akn:hc_1/p44 akn:hc_1/p45 akn:hc_1/p46 akn:hc_1/p47 akn:hc_1/p48 akn:hc_1/p49 akn:hc_1/p50 akn:hc_1/p53 akn:hc_1/p60 The table's title, its section headings ("compulsory subjects", "electives with special instructions", "all the other electives") and its column headings; the rows follow.

-- The table's rows: Bible (religious), 3 units (¶51-¶52); geography, 5
-- units, its questionnaire and its geotop (¶54-¶56); Land-of-Israel
-- studies, 5 units, likewise (¶57-¶59); and Bible in state-religious
-- education, 5 units (¶61-¶66). The corpus publishes the table as loose
-- lines with each row's cells out of order, so which figure sits in which
-- column is not something its text says (MMS-424). The figures are an
-- input until the corpus publishes the table and is re-synced; the notes
-- beside the rows are readable prose and are encoded below.
@ref akn:hc_1/p51 akn:hc_1/p52 akn:hc_1/p54 akn:hc_1/p55 akn:hc_1/p56 akn:hc_1/p57 akn:hc_1/p58 akn:hc_1/p59 akn:hc_1/p61 akn:hc_1/p66
@desc The rows of the attached table, one per printed row in the printed order. The corpus publishes this table scrambled (MMS-424), so the values are supplied from outside until the corpus is fixed and re-synced.
ASSUME `the updated rows` IS A LIST OF `reward row`

-- The geotop rows' note (¶55-¶56, ¶58-¶59): "this is the bagrut reward
-- for the geotop, as was customary before the reform" — the geotop's
-- reward in the reform is its pre-reform reward, unchanged.
@ref akn:hc_1/p55 akn:hc_1/p56 akn:hc_1/p58 akn:hc_1/p59
GIVEN `the pre-reform geotop reward` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the geotop reward in the reform` `the pre-reform geotop reward` IS
    `the pre-reform geotop reward`

-- The weight of the external examination each row's note states. The
-- column heading prints "70%" over the external part and "30%" over the
-- school-based one: the general split of circular תשע"ה/2, which the
-- religious Bible row follows; the three other subjects are this table's
-- "special instructions" and state their own weight beside the row
-- (geography 60/40, ¶54; Land-of-Israel studies 30/70, ¶57;
-- state-religious Bible 50/50, ¶61). The 50/50 note sits on the one row
-- under the heading "כל יתר מקצועות הבחירה" (¶60), state-religious Bible;
-- it is read as that row's weight, not as a new split for every other
-- elective, because ¶16 says the updates are in the subjects the table
-- lists.
@ref akn:hc_1/p47 akn:hc_1/p48 akn:hc_1/p54 akn:hc_1/p57 akn:hc_1/p61
GIVEN s IS A STRING
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `the external weight stated for` s IS
    IF s EQUALS "גיאוגרפיה" THEN 0.6
    ELSE IF s EQUALS "לימודי ארץ ישראל" THEN 0.3
         ELSE IF s EQUALS "תנ\"ך ממ\"ד" THEN 0.5
              ELSE 0.7

-- ¶16 and the table's title: the subjects the table lists have their
-- internal split updated. A part of a row's reward under the updated split;
-- NOTHING where the table leaves the cell blank.
@export default The part of the matriculation (bagrut) preparation reward that goes to the external examination or to the school-based assessment, in weekly hours or in percent, for a subject whose split the owners' circular 5779/9 updates from 1 September 2019
@ref akn:hc_1/p44 akn:hc_1/p16
GIVEN r IS A `reward row` @desc a row of the table (an input, see the table's rows)
      p IS A `part of the reward` @desc the external examination or the school-based assessment
      u IS A `unit of the reward` @desc weekly hours (ש"ש) or percent
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the reward for the part` r p u IS
    CONSIDER p
    WHEN `the external examination` THEN
        CONSIDER u
        WHEN `weekly hours` THEN r's `external, weekly hours`
        WHEN `percent` THEN r's `external, percent`
    WHEN `the school-based assessment` THEN
        CONSIDER u
        WHEN `weekly hours` THEN r's `school-based, weekly hours`
        WHEN `percent` THEN r's `school-based, percent`

GIVEN r IS A `reward row`, u IS A `unit of the reward`
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the whole reward` r u IS
    CONSIDER u
    WHEN `weekly hours` THEN r's `before the reform, weekly hours`
    WHEN `percent` THEN r's `before the reform, percent`

§§ `חלוקת חלק בין שני אירועי בחינה`

DECLARE `examination event` IS ONE OF
    `the first external questionnaire`
    `the second external questionnaire`
    `the first school-based event`
    `the second school-based event`

`all examination events` MEANS
    LIST `the first external questionnaire`, `the second external questionnaire`,
         `the first school-based event`, `the second school-based event`

-- The religious Bible row's note: two external questionnaires, the
-- external reward divided between them equally.
@ref akn:hc_1/p51 akn:hc_1/p52
GIVEN e IS AN `examination event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `religious Bible share of the external part` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the first external questionnaire` THEN 0.5
    WHEN `the second external questionnaire` THEN 0.5
    OTHERWISE 0

-- The state-religious Bible row's note: both parts are divided into two
-- questionnaires or examination events, the external one equally (25% of
-- the reward each), the school-based one into 20% and 30%. The note does
-- not say which school-based event takes which; the reading adopted
-- (F-2018-19_tashat_09-a) gives 20% to the first in order and 30% to the
-- second, following the order the note prints them in.
@ref akn:hc_1/p62 akn:hc_1/p63 akn:hc_1/p64 akn:hc_1/p65 akn:hc_1/p66
GIVEN e IS AN `examination event`
GIVETH A NUMBER
DECIDE `state-religious Bible share of the whole reward` e IS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `the first external questionnaire` THEN 0.25
    WHEN `the second external questionnaire` THEN 0.25
    WHEN `the first school-based event` THEN 0.20
    WHEN `the second school-based event` THEN 0.30

-- "יש לחלק את הגמול": the owners divide and pay the reward by the updated
-- split. When each part is paid is circular תשע"ה/2's rule, not this
-- circular's, so the duty here carries no deadline.
@ref akn:hc_1/p51 akn:hc_1/p63
GIVEN r IS A `reward row`, p IS A `part of the reward`
GIVETH A DEONTIC Party `reward action`
DECIDE `paying a part of the reward in weekly hours` r p IS
    PARTY `the employer`
    MUST  `pay the reward for the part` `hours`
          PROVIDED `hours` AT LEAST fromMaybe 0 (`the reward for the part` r p `weekly hours`)

§§ `Worked examples`

-- Findings.

-- F-2018-19_tashat_09-a: both orders of 20% and 30% fit the note, and they
-- give the first school-based event different rewards.
`the school-based shares as printed` MEANS LIST 0.20, 0.30
`the school-based part of the state-religious Bible reward` MEANS
    `state-religious Bible share of the whole reward` `the first school-based event`
    PLUS `state-religious Bible share of the whole reward` `the second school-based event`
`the school-based split names no event for each share` MEANS
        sum `the school-based shares as printed` EQUALS `the school-based part of the state-religious Bible reward`
    AND NOT (at `the school-based shares as printed` 0 EQUALS at `the school-based shares as printed` 1)
#ASSERT `the school-based split names no event for each share`

-- Checks a row of the table must pass, and examples. The table is an
-- input, so the rows below are PLACEHOLDERS with round invented figures,
-- not the table's values.

GIVEN x IS A MAYBE NUMBER, y IS A MAYBE NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE NUMBER
DECIDE `the sum of` x y IS
    CONSIDER x
    WHEN NOTHING THEN y
    WHEN JUST a THEN
        CONSIDER y
        WHEN NOTHING THEN JUST a
        WHEN JUST b THEN JUST (a PLUS b)

-- A row's external and school-based parts add up to its whole reward, in
-- weekly hours and in percent.
GIVEN r IS A `reward row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the row's parts add up` r IF
    all (GIVEN u YIELD
            `the sum of` (`the reward for the part` r `the external examination` u)
                         (`the reward for the part` r `the school-based assessment` u)
            EQUALS `the whole reward` r u)
        (LIST `weekly hours`, `percent`)

-- A questionnaire row's external part is the weight its note states.
GIVEN r IS A `reward row`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the external part is the stated weight` r IF
    CONSIDER `the reward for the part` r `the external examination` `weekly hours`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN TRUE
    WHEN JUST e THEN
        CONSIDER `the whole reward` r `weekly hours`
        WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
        WHEN JUST w THEN e EQUALS w TIMES `the external weight stated for` (r's `subject`)

-- PLACEHOLDER rows (invented figures): a geography questionnaire of 10
-- weekly hours split 60/40, and a geotop row with only a school-based cell.
`a placeholder geography questionnaire row` MEANS
    `reward row` "גיאוגרפיה" 5 "שאלון"
        (JUST 10) (JUST 10)
        (JUST 6) (JUST 6)
        (JUST 4) (JUST 4)

`a placeholder geotop row` MEANS
    `reward row` "גיאוגרפיה" 5 "גיאוטופ"
        (JUST 1) NOTHING
        NOTHING NOTHING
        (JUST 1) NOTHING

`the placeholder rows` MEANS
    LIST `a placeholder geography questionnaire row`, `a placeholder geotop row`

#ASSERT all `the row's parts add up` `the placeholder rows`
#ASSERT all `the external part is the stated weight` `the placeholder rows`
#ASSERT `the reward for the part` `a placeholder geography questionnaire row` `the external examination` `weekly hours` EQUALS JUST 6
#ASSERT `the reward for the part` `a placeholder geotop row` `the external examination` `percent` EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `the geotop reward in the reform` 1 EQUALS 1

-- The state-religious Bible shares make up the whole reward, half external.
#ASSERT sum (map `state-religious Bible share of the whole reward` `all examination events`) EQUALS 1
#ASSERT `state-religious Bible share of the whole reward` `the first external questionnaire` TIMES 10 EQUALS 2.5
#ASSERT `religious Bible share of the external part` `the second external questionnaire` TIMES 10 EQUALS 5
#ASSERT `the updated split applies to the year beginning` (Date 1 9 2019)
#ASSERT NOT `the updated split applies to the year beginning` (Date 1 9 2018)

#TRACE `paying a part of the reward in weekly hours` `a placeholder geography questionnaire row` `the school-based assessment` AT 0 WITH
    PARTY `the employer` DOES `pay the reward for the part` 4 AT 1
